    "description_en": "Golden green-plantain balls with melted cheese, served with a fried egg and fresh tomato salsa.",
    "name_en": "Ecuadorian bolón de verde with cheese and fried egg",
    "base_en": "green-plantain balls",
    "ingredients_en": "4 large green plantains, 200 g mild white melting cheese, 40 g butter, 4 eggs, 3 medium tomatoes, 1/2 small red onion, 2 tbsp lime juice, 20 ml oil, 1 tsp salt, 1/4 tsp black pepper",
    "recipe_en": "<p>Peel and cut the plantains, then boil in salted water for 15 minutes.</p><p>Drain and mash with the butter to a firm mixture.</p><p>Add the grated cheese and shape 8 balls.</p><p>Brown them in a lightly oiled pan on all sides.</p><p>Mix the tomatoes with onion, lime, salt and pepper.</p><p>Fry the eggs.</p><p>Serve two bolón per person with egg and tomato salsa.</p>",
